curl -I LINK      | HEAD request, headers only
curl -i LINK      | GET request + headers + body
curl -v LINK      | Verbose: request + response headers + body
curl -H "" LINK   | Send custom request headers
curl -L LINK      | Redirest
curl -D FILE LINK | Demp response headers to file
curl -b FILE LINK | Send cookies from file
curl -c FILE LINK | Save response cookies to file
curl -v LINK      | Debugging - '>' are sent headers, '<' are received headers, '*' are curl info messages
